    "result_text": "Tests are green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with the finding \u2014 the \"E.164, else raw, else empty\" fallback was duplicated in three places \u2014 and applied the \"Better\" fix, placing the concept in the unit that already owns telephone normalization:\n\n1. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 added a `toComparable(String)` method: returns the E.164 form, else the raw value unchanged, else an empty string (never throws). This is the single home for \"comparable telephone\".\n\n2. **`IdentityKeyNormalizer.derive`** \u2014 replaced its inline `toE164`-plus-fallback block with `TelephoneNormalizer.toComparable(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 deleted my newly added `normalizedTelephone` helper and routed both `assignPossibleDuplicate` and `deriveCustomerCode` through `TelephoneNormalizer.toComparable`, eliminating the third copy.\n\nAll three call sites now share one implementation, and behavior is unchanged (`toComparable` produces exactly what each previously computed). `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
