    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe bulk of this change is clean and well-integrated:\n- `assignPossibleDuplicate` mirrors the sibling create-pipeline helpers (`countNamesakes`, `assignHousehold`, `rejectWhenDuplicateIdentity`) in shape, naming, normalization approach, and doc style, and is inserted at the right point in `createOwner` (after the hard-duplicate check, before persist).\n- The `OwnerMapper.possibleDuplicate` default method is a faithful copy of the `bulkSignupWarning` pattern; leaving `possibleDuplicateOf` to MapStruct's direct field mapping (like `namesakeCount`/`householdMemberCount`) is idiomatic \u2014 no explicit mapper needed.\n- Entity fields, getters/setters, the four schema variants, and the OpenAPI additions are all consistent with the existing owners table/schema conventions.\n\nOne duplication finding:\n\n**`normalizedTelephone` re-introduces a third copy of the \"E.164, else raw, else empty\" telephone logic.** The exact same fallback block already exists inline in `deriveCustomerCode` (ClinicServiceImpl.java:490-493) *in this same class*, and again in `IdentityKeyNormalizer.derive` (lines 48-51). The new helper's own Javadoc even says it uses \"the same handling the identity key uses\" \u2014 acknowledging the duplication rather than removing it.\n\nConcrete, actionable fix (pick one):\n- Minimal: have `deriveCustomerCode` call the new `normalizedTelephone(owner)` helper instead of keeping its own inline copy, so there is a single copy within `ClinicServiceImpl`.\n- Better: promote this canonicalization to a `TelephoneNormalizer` method (e.g. `toComparable(String)` returning E.164, else the raw value, else empty), and route `assignPossibleDuplicate`, `deriveCustomerCode`, and `IdentityKeyNormalizer.derive` through it. That puts the \"comparable telephone\" concept in the unit that already owns telephone normalization and eliminates all three copies.",
